1. [MAJOR] `phases/phase-088/REPORT.md:263` — the quoted gate block is not a run of the gate over this phase's diff: its own line `PASS diff substance: +1857 -70 (min +5)` matches neither the committed half of this phase (`+1626 −70`: 175+353+334+68+202+12+190+232+28+12+20 added, 17+1+15+18+4+2+13 removed) nor the committed-plus-working-tree diff (`+2004 −114`, the uncommitted half being +378/−44) — so either the block was produced against a different tree/base, or `REPORT.md:241` ("It was run with `RBOPS_BASE_REF=c6e9837`") is wrong. The block also carries `WARN report claims 1976 passing, actual run has 1980` (line 294), which `REPORT.md:302-311` itself explains as the gate having read the pipeline's stale copy of the report — and then asserts, without having observed it, that the pipeline's real run "answers `PASS reported test count (1980) matches actual (1980)`". Why it matters: `phases/phase-088/FINDINGS.md:200-204` (written in this same round) states the rule this report breaks — "A quoted gate output is not evidence; the gate's own output is… Paste only what the run in this tree printed" — and says round 1 was rejected for exactly this. The Gates table's central "the gate passed" row rests on a block that cannot be the gate's output for this tree. Fix: after the table says 1980, re-run `RBOPS_BASE_REF=c6e9837 ../rbops/verify.sh phase-088` in this checkout (copying this tree's `phases/phase-088/REPORT.md` into the path the gate reads first) and paste that output verbatim; if the block's numbers cannot be reproduced, drop the quote rather than explain it. — VERIFIED by tracing the change set's own diffstat (the numbers above) against the quoted `+1857 −70`; I could not re-run the gate (read-only reviewer).
2. [MINOR] `phases/phase-088/REPORT.md:24` — the per-file line-count table does not match the diff it summarises: `tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs` is stated as `+252 −18` while the diff is `+260 −26` (232/18 committed + 28/8 uncommitted), and `tests/loop_bounds_test.rs` is stated as `+203 −17` while the diff is `+202 −17`. The other six rows match. Why it matters: this table is the phase's own account of the diff and is the first thing a reader checks against `git diff --numstat`; two of eight rows are wrong, in a phase whose whole thesis is "don't take a number on trust, measure it". Fix: regenerate the column from `git diff --numstat c6e9837` (base → working tree, which also covers the round-2 files `tests/failure_channel_test.rs` +146 and `phases/phase-088/scan.py` +334 that the table lists without counts).
3. [MINOR] `phases/phase-088/FINDINGS.md:162` — the finding that "`phases/phase-087/REPORT.md:137` records a gate count the tree does not have… The 201-test gap is in phase-087's row" is not supported by the comparison it makes: phase-087's 1766 was measured on phase-087's own tree, while1967 was measured on this phase's base `c6e9837`, a later tree that also carries phase-089's delivery (the `ACKNOWLEDGED` entry `bf9ffc33…` in `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs:169` records `+1068/-15, 11 files, +381/-15 under src/`, where the unit tests live) — so 1766 → 1967 is accounted for by the intervening work, not by an error in phase-087's row. Why it matters: the phase publishes the accusation as a FINDING and tells the next phase that "a report that carries a stale count is a trap", which puts a false mark on a neighbouring phase's record and teaches the wrong lesson. Fix: either drop §6, or check out phase-087's own base commit and measure the suite there, as the report already prescribes elsewhere ("re-measure it rather than add to it").

